# Read by BaseAgent._loadIgnorePatterns() (sast-engine/rules/base-agent.js).
#
# Why: the pattern rules are made of the strings they look for, so scanning this repo with
# itself makes every rule report itself. In auth-bypass-agent.js the regex /\bDEBUG\s*=\s*True\b/
# matches the title 'Django: DEBUG = True' on the line above it. Measured: 107 of 134 findings
# came from these two directories, and all 40 that reached adjudication were false positives.
#
# Scope is the rule corpus only. enumerate.js, ast-extract.js, remediation-apply.js and
# commands/ stay in scope deliberately — remediation-apply.js is the one function here that
# writes to disk. Do not widen this to "sast-engine/".
#
# Known side effect: whole-tree analyses now see a smaller repo. UNUSED_DEPENDENCY reports
# fast-glob as unused; it is not, it is imported by five files under rules/. Treat a
# low-severity UNUSED_DEPENDENCY hit here with suspicion. UnusedGuardAgent's reference counting
# has the same blind spot.
#
# The reasoning passes are unaffected — they read the target with their own Read/Grep/Glob.

sast-engine/rules/
sast-engine/utils/

